                            'Lenin treats the opposition as a question of starting point, not of wording. Put matter first and treat sensation as its reflection, and you have materialism; put sensation first and treat things as its complexes, and you have idealism. That is why Mach’s doctrine is a rehash of Berkeleianism.',
